    "Stem": "Controller Elena Kowalski at Bridgeway Imports has a €2,000,000 account payable to a German supplier due in 60 days. The spot rate is $1.12/€, and the 60-day forward rate is $1.135/€. Bridgeway can also borrow dollars at 5.50% or euros at 3.80% (both annualized). Ms. Kowalski must compare the cost of a forward hedge versus a money market hedge. Which analysis correctly identifies the cheaper hedging strategy?",
