    "Stem": "CEO Sarah Novak at GlobalTech Industries is evaluating a manufacturing investment in an emerging market country. The project has an expected local-currency NPV of $45M, but the country recently experienced a change in government, and the new administration has proposed raising the corporate tax rate from 20% to 30% and imposing new restrictions on profit repatriation. GlobalTech's WACC for domestic projects is 9.00%. Ms. Novak must determine how to incorporate country risk into the investment analysis. Which approach is correct under corporate finance theory?",
